{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["And here it adds: <b>and your ox and your donkey</b>, to explain that it is also forbidden in the labor of the land, which is the livelihood of man, as in the manner it says (Exodus 34:21), \"in plowing and in harvest you shall cease.\" And here it says, \"that your male slave and your female slave may rest as you do,\" and \"you shall remember that you were a slave,\" etc., to explain that in it He commands regarding the rest of the slave like yourself, because you were a slave and HaShem granted you rest, and you too shall grant rest to your slave. Now the reason is: when your male slave and your female slave rest as you do, you will remember that you were a slave, etc."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:45:29.780687049Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}